/T (DRAINING THE TANK   If the tank is to be replaced, ensure the site is appropriate for safe drainage. Draining can be performed by connecting a hose to the cold water inlet and running it to a suitable drain point. To prevent the formation of a partial vacuum during draining, it is necessary to disconnect the hot water outlet or open the Pressure and Temperature Relief \(PTR\) valve.  )
/E (DRAINING THE TANK   If the tank is to be replaced, ensure the site is appropriate for safe drainage. Draining can be performed by connecting a hose to the cold water inlet and running it to a suitable drain point. To prevent the formation of a partial vacuum during draining, it is necessary to disconnect the hot water outlet or open the Pressure and Temperature Relief \(PTR\) valve.  )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [17]
